# ==============================================================================
# Confining Wall Snippet (fix wall/lj93) — liquid/solid interface restraint
# Apply when: liquid electrolyte in a slab cell must be kept away from the cell
#             boundary (e.g. between two electrodes), WITHOUT opening a vacuum gap
# ==============================================================================
# USAGE:
# - zlo/zhi EDGE: the wall position (box coordinate, A with units metal).
# - epsilon sigma cutoff: 9-3 Lennard-Jones wall parameters; typical starting
#   values epsilon ~ 0.1-1.0 eV (units metal), sigma ~ 2.5-3.5 A — please adjust
#   to your system.
# - Difference vs. vacuum: a wall is a SOFT potential (no boundary change, keeps
#   p p p periodicity + kspace); a vacuum gap uses boundary p p f and breaks
#   long-range Coulombics unless kspace_modify slab is set.
# - ORDER: define walls BEFORE fix shake if both are used (shake must come last).

# >>> USER: set EDGE to your box z-extents and tune epsilon/sigma <<<
fix             wall_lo all wall/lj93 zlo 1.0 0.5 3.0 2.5
fix             wall_hi all wall/lj93 zhi 39.0 0.5 3.0 2.5
#                                  EDGE  epsilon sigma cutoff
